Title: The Spare Key
Credit: original short, written as the WP7 benchmark
Author: Claude (draft)
Format: 3 scenes x 16 s (each scene = 2 Flow generations of 8 s, one shot each), English dialogue
Tests: three people in one room; a prop handled exactly once; a sneer; rain outside the window; a flashback
Gate1: APPROVED by Tech Lead under Owner-delegated authority 2026-11-01

INT. MOTHER'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

[[look: old family kitchen, yellow pendant lamp over a wooden table, faded floral wallpaper, rain streaking the window over the sink, the room itself dry]]

AUNT ROSA, sixties, silver hair in a bun, black dress, sits at the table. ELENA, early forties, stands by the counter beside her. In the doorway opposite stands her younger brother MARCUS, late thirties, brown leather jacket. A small brass key on a red ribbon lies on the table.

MARCUS
So she left the house to you.

MARCUS walks to the table, picks up the brass key, and puts it in his jacket pocket. He looks at ELENA with a thin sneer.

MARCUS
Mom always liked you best.

INT. MOTHER'S KITCHEN - THAT MORNING (FLASHBACK)

[[marker: title card "That morning"; warm sunlight, no rain]]

ROSA and ELENA sit across the table from each other. The brass key on its ribbon lies between them. ROSA slides an old iron key across the table to ELENA.

ROSA
The brass one opens nothing.

ELENA closes her fingers around the iron key and nods once.

ELENA
He'll take it anyway.

INT. MOTHER'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

ELENA looks at MARCUS, calm.

ELENA
Keep it, Marcus.

ROSA looks up at MARCUS from her chair.

ROSA
Your mother changed the locks.

The sneer leaves MARCUS's face. Rain runs down the window behind him.
